  "notes": "A piano-first classical/gospel-soul hybrid, and the research calls her \"the least programmed artist in this lane\", 2001–2009. Tempo is \"60–93\", with the signature record notated 12/8 at a \"free\" 60 and a straight 4/4 band at 75–93; the mode is 75, the sourced \"A Woman's Worth\" reading. The engine has no compound meter, so the **12/8 compound feel is encoded as `swing.grid` `8th` at `amount` 0.667 — full triplet** — which is the only honest mapping available and is called out here because it is a translation, not a measurement. Three drum deltas come from the entry: Kerry \"Krucial\" Brothers \"programs a hip-hop kit *under* a triplet piano feel — kick on 1, snare on 2&4… no busy hats, and the swing carried by the piano rather than the drum grid\", so the hat lane drops to an 8th base at 0.1 fill density with a `16T` roll vocabulary, the snare sits 3–8 ms behind the grid, and \"live drum and hand-percussion layers\" become a four-lane conga/tambourine/shaker/rim bed with `quantizeStrength` at 0.6. Harmony is the identifying half: \"minor blues cycles with ii–V–i, borrowed IV and passing diminished chords, 4-bar (not 2-bar) harmonic loops\" — all four are authored, including an `i`–`IV` family for the borrowed major subdominant and a `vii°` passing family, with `susOrDimProb` raised. \"Contralto-alto lead with gospel melisma; note density high\" is the 4–11 density and the wide register; \"live violin or strings as countermelody\" is the counter at +12 with a 0.5 density. The bass is \"acoustic-piano left hand and an electric/synth bass doubling it; no 808 sub\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every velocity and density number and the triplet mapping above. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode blues/gospel\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
